---
import UtilityLayout from "../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import UtilityApp from "../../components/UtilityApp.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Fix mixed spreadsheet dates"
  description="Clean up a list of dates, with unclear values kept visible for review."
  slug="fix-excel-dates"
>
  <p class="notice">
    For date text only. Excel serial numbers, timestamps and spreadsheet files
    are not supported.
  </p>
  <UtilityApp tool="dates" />
  <details class="prose tool-help">
    <summary>How this tool works &amp; limits</summary>
    <h2>Formatting a cell is not the same as repairing its date</h2>
    <p>
      Spreadsheet imports can interpret some dates as numbers and leave others
      as text. Paste original date strings here to preview their meaning before
      another import. Unspecified numeric dates such as 03/04/2026 remain for
      review; selecting day-first or month-first is an explicit interpretation,
      not a cosmetic display change.
    </p>
    <h2>What gets preserved?</h2>
    <p>
      Year-only and year-month values retain their precision. Invalid dates,
      missing information and unsupported formats are reported alongside the
      original text. The tool does not invent a day, fix corrupted historical
      values, or infer a timezone.
    </p>
    <h2>Supported input and importing the result</h2>
    <p>
      ISO dates, four-digit-year day/month or month/day strings, and English
      month names are supported. Excel serial numbers, two-digit years and
      timestamps are outside this first version. Import the output using your
      spreadsheet’s import workflow and explicitly select the intended date
      convention. CSV does not store spreadsheet formatting, so reopening it can
      trigger fresh inference by Excel. Inspect your import preview.
    </p>
    <p>
      Jev is optional: use it when the source context needs interpretation, not
      for ordinary calendar arithmetic. It suggests a convention from your
      description; it cannot determine missing facts from an ambiguous date
      alone.
    </p>
  </details>
</UtilityLayout>
